# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Richard Tran et al. (2023). The Open Catalyst 2022 (OC22) Dataset and Challenges for Oxide Electrocatalysts.
#   ACS Catalysis. doi:10.1021/acscatal.2c05426  arXiv:2206.08917v3
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2206.08917v3 (sha256 cbb94c1b0ca94552...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 220 (Dataset/benchmark). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/tran2023.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the OC22 data set introduced here (62,331 DFT relaxations
# of oxide surfaces with and without adsorbates) and the S2EF-Total test
# errors of the baseline GNNs whose methods are in the registry (Table 3):
# SchNet, DimeNet++, PaiNN, GemNet-dT and GemNet-OC trained on OC22 only,
# jointly with OC20 subsets, or fine-tuned from OC20 checkpoints.
# SpinConv and ForceNet (not registry methods), the median baseline,
# IS2RE-Total, IS2RS, the fine-tuning fractions (Table 4) and the OC20
# comparisons of the SI are not encoded.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
