###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Over 240 million core-hours were used to create the data set (Sec. on
# structure relaxation). Model training cost is not given in the main text.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Introduces the OC22 data set; its level of theory is entered in the data-set registry from this paper. The origin-paper stub of this paper is removed from origin-papers.csv now that it is encoded.
# - OC22 energies are DFT total energies (not adsorption energies); the energy MAEs are per structure in eV. SchNet, DimeNet++, PaiNN and GemNet-dT use a 6 A cutoff with at most 50 neighbours 'unless otherwise noted'; GemNet-OC uses interaction-specific cutoffs (SI).
# - PaiNN is modified to predict forces directly; GemNet-dT and GemNet-OC are settings of the registry method GemNet; DimeNet++ is recorded under DimeNet.
# - The fine-tuned models start from public OC20 adsorption-energy checkpoints; their base models are recorded in the encoding input. Hyperparameters beyond the cutoff are in the SI (Table 13) and are not encoded.
# - Force cosine and EFwT are not accuracy metrics of the schema.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/tran2023.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

# --- BenchmarkResult labels (generated by artifacts/scripts/add_result_labels.py; do not edit) ---
<https://w3id.org/mlips/entity/result-dimenetpp-tran2023> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "DimeNet++ OC22 S2EF-Total model (OC22-only) on Oxide surfaces (slabs) with and without OER-relevant adsorbates (OC22)" .
<https://w3id.org/mlips/entity/result-gemnet-dt-ft-tran2023> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GemNet-dT OC22 S2EF-Total model (fine-tuned OC20 -> OC22) on Oxide surfaces (slabs) with and without OER-relevant adsorbates (OC22)" .
